# A field's DIRECTIVES are codegen inputs, so schema-diff's `compare_fields` has
# to compare them and not just field names, field types and argument types.
# Adding `@semanticNonNull` to `Query.greeting` must therefore produce an
# `ObjectChanged` entry for `Query`.
#
# The unrelated `Unrelated` object is what makes the gap observable: without it
# `diff()` ends up with an empty change list and returns `GenericChange`
# (-> `Unsafe` -> full rebuild), which masks the problem. With it, a
# `compare_fields` that ignored directives would report only `ObjectAdded`,
# which `get_safety` classifies as `Safe`, so `build_programs` would pick
# `BuildMode::Incremental` and never recompile `fooFragment`.
#
# `greeting` types as `string` (semantic-non-null is honored because the
# fragment is `@throwOnFieldError`), and the incremental build must agree with a
# clean build rather than keeping the stale `string | null | undefined`.

//- foo.js
graphql`
  fragment fooFragment on Query @throwOnFieldError {
    greeting
  }
`

